# RORA: OR register - 10-bit mask instruction
# YAML: mask "1111_1111_1100_0000", opcode "145400" (octal)
# Logical OR operation with optional sub-instructions
#
# Basic operation: dr ← dr | sr
# With sub-instructions:
# - CLD: Use zero instead of destination register
# - CM1: Use 1's complement of source register
#
# Instruction combinations:
# RORA <sr> <dr>           dr ← dr | sr
# RORA CLD <sr> <dr>       dr ← sr
# RORA CM1 <sr> <dr>       dr ← dr | ~sr
# RORA CM1 CLD <sr> <dr>   dr ← ~sr
#
# P-code implementation:
# local src_val:2 = sr;
# local dst_val:2 = dr;
# if (CM1) src_val = ~src_val;
# if (CLD) dst_val = 0;
# dr = dst_val | src_val;
# # Update flags based on result
# STS[Q] = dr s< 0;  # Sign flag
# STS[C] = 0;        # Clear carry
# STS[O] = 0;        # Clear overflow
#
# SLEIGH Limitation: Cannot implement due to 10-bit mask
# Manual implementation would require sub-tables for sub-instruction combinations